  "question": {
    "text": "A block moving horizontally on a smooth surface with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> splits into two equal parts. If one of the parts moves at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in the same direction, then the fractional&nbsp;change in the kinetic energy will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/efef3b84-8863-4679-9eac-3046b0e1563c-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 109px;\" /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math><br />Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>20</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>60</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>40</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>800</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>40</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3200</mn></math><br />Fractional change <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
